-- title:
--   Generic points of the second special-fibre component have codimension one
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \geq 5$ with $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a $p$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K \subseteq L((q))$ be the intermediate field [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of the Laurent series field generated by the coefficientwise images under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $\mathbb{Q}$-rational $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, and let $j \in K$ be the element whose image in $L((q))$ is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), assumed nonzero. Write $X$ for the two-chart integral model [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of `fFin` and `fInf` gluing the affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgFin A K j` and $\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgInf A K j`, and `toBase` (equivalently [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252)) for its structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$, given on the two charts by the structural algebra maps from $A$. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ with an $A$-algebra structure, and let $X_k$ denote the pullback of `modelTo` along $\operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} A$. Assume given schemes $C_1, C_2$ proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral over $\operatorname{Spec} k$, together with morphisms $i_1, i_2$ from $C_1, C_2$ to $X_k$ commuting with the structure morphisms to $\operatorname{Spec} k$ and whose underlying scheme morphisms are closed immersions, such that every point of $X_k$ lies in the set-theoretic image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$, such that the pullback of $i_1$ along $i_2$ is reduced with $\operatorname{Nat.card}$ equal to some $n > 0$; assume further a section $\varepsilon$ of `modelTo` over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, sections $\varepsilon_1, \varepsilon_2$ of $c_1, c_2$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$ with $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ equal to the base-changed section `sectionBaseChange k ε`, and an element $w$ of [`ModularCurve.IntegralWeightOneForm k M`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L16), i.e. a weight-one modular form on $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with an integral power series realising its $q$-expansion and having nonvanishing reduction `intSeriesC k`. The conclusion is: for every $\varpi \in A$ generating $\mathfrak{m}_A$ and every $\xi \in C_2$ whose closure is all of $C_2$, writing $z$ for the image of $\xi$ under $i_2$ followed by the projection $X_k \to X$, the germ at $z$ of the global section of $X$ obtained from $\varpi$ by the inverse of `Scheme.ΓSpecIso` and the map on global sections induced by `toBase` lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$, and $\operatorname{ringKrullDim} \mathcal{O}_{X,z} \leq 1$.
--
--   The two assertions are precisely the hypotheses — that $z$ lies on the special fibre, and that the local ring there has Krull dimension at most one — under which the local ring of the two-chart integral model at $z$ is identified with a valuation ring of $K$; in this way each irreducible component of the geometric special fibre of the model of $X_1(Mp)$ over the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$ yields a codimension-one point of the model. It is used in the construction of the valuation subring and the identification of its residue data in [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_valuationSubring_algEquiv_fractionRing_tensorProduct_of_curveModel_snd_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_valuationSubring_algEquiv_fractionRing_tensorProduct_of_curveModel_snd_twoChartModel_x1_mul).
